# Canvas.Pdf

A minimal, extensible PDF generation engine built in C# (.NET 10), without external PDF libraries.

## Features

- Create PDF documents and multiple pages
- Draw text with standard fonts
- Paragraph rendering with wrapping and alignment (`Left`, `Center`, `Right`, `Justify`)
- Draw vector primitives (`Line`, `Rectangle`, `RoundedRectangle`, `Circle`, `Polygon`)
- Configure stroke style (`PdfStrokeStyle`) for dashed lines, line caps, and line joins
- Draw images (`PNG`, `JPEG`) including PNG transparency (alpha)
- Preserve aspect ratio with image layout helpers (`DrawImageScaledToWidth`, `DrawImageScaledToHeight`, `DrawImageFit`, `DrawImageFitCenter`)
- Color support:
  - RGB (`PdfColor`)
  - Grayscale (`PdfGrayColor`)
  - CMYK (`PdfCmykColor`)
- Document metadata (`Title`, `Author`, `Subject`, etc.)

## Quick Start

```csharp
using Canvas.Pdf;

var doc = new PdfDocument(defaultFont: PdfStandardFonts.FromStyle(PdfFontFamily.Times));
doc.Info.Title = "Hello Canvas.Pdf";

var page = doc.AddPage();
page.DrawText("Hello World", x: 100, y: 700, fontSize: 14);
page.DrawImage("logo.png", x: 100, y: 620, width: 120, height: 80);

doc.Save("output.pdf");
```

## Demo

Run the included console demo:

```powershell
dotnet run --project Canvas/Canvas.csproj
```

The output file is generated at:
`Canvas/bin/Debug/net10.0/output.pdf`

